  "cdse:collection_description": "Dry Matter Productivity (DMP) represents the overall growth rate or dry biomass increase of the vegetation — that is, the amount of new dry matter produced per unit of time. DMP is closely related to ecosystem Net Primary Production (NPP) but uses units adapted to agro-statistical applications (kg/ha/day). Estimates are generated at 10-day intervals at global scale, with a spatial resolution of about 300 m, and the time series extends from January 2014 to the present.",
